    "scenesThatPass": [
      "ELLIE: \"What's surprising is: people don't see what they're not looking for.\"\nASTER: \"The obvious unseen.\"",
      "ELLIE: I'll be re-open for business soon enough. I mean this can't go on much longer.\nASTER: \"I've been thinking about what you said about 'seeing' and 'not seeing.'\"",
      "ASTER: \"I had a painting teacher once tell me that the difference between a 'good' painting and a 'great' painting...\"\nASTER: \"...is typically five strokes. And they are usually the five boldest strokes in the painting. The question of course...\"\nASTER: \"Is which five strokes?\"\nELLIE: \"After one's slaved away at making a \"pretty good\" painting, the last thing you'd want to do is...\"",
      "ELLIE: \"...make a BOLD STROKE and potentially...\"\nASTER: \"...ruin everything. That's why I gave up painting.\" \\\nASTER: \"Still.. I wonder if that is how I'm living my life.\"",
      "ELLIE: \"Oh so that's your boldest stroke?\" \\\nASTER: \"I'm into the slow build! What was \\ that?\" \\\nELLIE: \"Decisiveness. But please... take \\ all the time you need to be bold.\" \\\nASTER: \"Is THIS bold enough for you...?\""
    ]
